},{"text":" passes through ","type":"text"},{"code":"a","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each reachable vertex but the root has an immediate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dominator, its closest strict dominator, which is its parent in the tree.","type":"text"}],"title":"DominatorTree","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DominatorTree"}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/dominatortree","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DominatorTree"}]},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/KComponents":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KComponents"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/kcomponents","abstract":[{"text":"The k-components of an undirected graph (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k ≥ 1,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the maximal sets of vertices whose induced subgraph is k-vertex-connected, that is, has more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than k vertices and stays connected after removing any k − 1 of them. The 1-components are the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"connected components with an edge, the 2-components the blocks of three or more vertices; every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"k-component lies inside a (k − 1)-component. Components at one level may share fewer than k"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"KComponents"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connecti